  phase('google','Google Play first','Build 4 submitted / awaiting Google review','Shared',"<p><strong>Production 1.0.0 (4) has been submitted for Google review with the owner’s approval.</strong> Internal testing remains Active on build 4. The app is not publicly released. <a href='evidence/production-preflight-2026-11-10.json'>Current 10 November preflight</a>.</p><div class='step'><input id='task-google-build' type='checkbox' data-task><div><label for='task-google-build'>Use verified build 4<span class='owner'>Ready</span></label><p><a href='https://play.google.com/apps/internaltest/4700802560351016013'>Internal-test install link</a>. Existing tester list retained; version 4 is also the only production candidate. No new upload/build was needed.</p></div></div><div class='step'><input id='task-google-access' type='checkbox' data-task><div><label for='task-google-access'>Keep dedicated reviewer access available<span class='owner'>Verified</span></label><p>Private sign-in instructions remain saved. Public HTTPS reviewer login and identity passed on 10 November. Credentials are excluded from this release folder.</p></div></div><div class='step'><input id='task-google-declarations' type='checkbox' data-task><div><label for='task-google-declarations'>Keep listing and declarations accurate<span class='owner'>Complete</span></label><p>App content says \u201cYou\u2019re all caught up.\u201d Required English listing fields, Business category, India targeting, 18+ audience, trader status, privacy/deletion URLs, Data safety and foreground-service declaration are saved. Public policy/deletion pages returned HTTP 200.</p></div></div><div class='step'><input id='task-google-production' type='checkbox' data-task><div><label for='task-google-production'>Production validation and quick checks<span class='owner'>Passed</span></label><p>Zero blocking errors. One nonblocking missing-deobfuscation warning; minification disabled. Google\u2019s quick checks completed and changes can now be sent for review. <a href='evidence/ux-build-4/production-build-4-validation.png'>Validation screenshot</a>.</p></div></div><div class='step'><input id='task-google-submit' type='checkbox' data-task><div><label for='task-google-submit'>Submit only after owner instruction<span class='owner'>Pending</span></label><p>All 11 changes were submitted with owner approval. Managed publishing is off, so approved changes publish automatically under the saved full India rollout. Preserve reviewer/backend, policy pages and video throughout review. GitHub push is authorized and awaiting authentication.</p></div></div>");
  const iosName = fs.readdirSync(path.join(root,'ios')).find(name=>name.endsWith('.xcodeproj'))?.replace('.xcodeproj','') || 'InsightScoop';
  const archive=`xcodebuild -workspace ios/${iosName}.xcworkspace -scheme ${iosName} -configuration Release -destination 'generic/platform=iOS' -archivePath builds/InsightScoop.xcarchive archive\nxcodebuild -exportArchive -archivePath builds/InsightScoop.xcarchive -exportOptionsPlist release/insight-scoop/store/ExportOptions.example.plist -exportPath builds/ios-store`;
  phase('signing','Signed release candidates',`Android versionCode ${uiCandidateBuild} ready / Apple later`,'Codex',`<p>The current Android candidate is <code>artifacts/InsightScoop-1.0.0-${uiCandidateBuild}.aab</code>, signed with the existing upload certificate. The binary validator checks package/version, signature, all four ABIs, 54 ELF64 library alignments, restricted permissions and bundled policy text. ${link('Final verification',uiRefresh ? 'evidence/green-ui-build-3/verification.json' : 'evidence/google-release-2026-11-06/verification.json')}.</p>${step('signing-backup','Keep an encrypted upload-key backup off this Mac','You','Keys and passwords remain outside Git and the release ZIP; retain the existing key for future Play uploads.')}${step('signing-device','Keep the final Android phone result recorded',uiRefresh ? 'Build 3 phone QA pending' : 'Owner-reported pass','Owner installed build 2 through Play internal testing and reports everything worked and uploaded. Earlier native/emulator/deletion checks remain separately recorded. This report does not certify every device or edge case.')}<p>The earlier iOS archive is development signed. App Store export and the Account Holder agreement remain a later task; this round focuses on Google Play.</p>`);
  phase('verification','Final device and release checks','Local checks passed','Shared',`${step('baseline','Keep the physical baseline in context','Recorded','Owner reports Android and iOS recording/playback/upload success before the deletion changes. This remains baseline evidence; account deletion on a final signed physical-device build is still pending.')}${step('current-tests','Record the latest local verification','Done locally','Passed: 67 frontend regression tests, 68 backend tests including 9 disposable PostgreSQL integration tests, TypeScript, current unsigned iOS Release build, and Android ARM64 native Release/Debug builds. The current Android Release APK opened on an API 36 emulator. These are local builds; store signing and full release architecture validation remain pending.')}<div class='detail'><strong>Deletion flow and account isolation passed on both platforms.</strong><p>Cancel, wrong password, explicit confirmation, accepted deletion, sign-out and restart were checked. The other account’s data stayed safe. Android additionally verified real SecureStore token removal, surviving-account login, local native video playback and another session restore after restart. The iOS simulator shell used camera/SecureStore substitutes. Both used real disposable local PostgreSQL with mocked AWS/provider calls.</p><p>${link('iOS deletion evidence','evidence/deletion-ios/index.html')} · ${link('Android deletion evidence','evidence/deletion-android/index.html')} · ${link('Android native build summary','evidence/deletion-android/native-build-summary.txt')} · ${link('Current verification record','evidence/verification.json')}</p></div><p>Earlier branding/consent UI evidence: ${link('Empty sign-in','evidence/current-ui/01-sign-in-empty.png')} · ${link('Privacy reader','evidence/current-ui/02-privacy-policy.png')} · ${link('Terms reader','evidence/current-ui/03-terms-of-use.png')}. These reference captures predate account deletion.</p>${step('signed-device','Recheck the final signed candidate','Shared','Check fresh install/update, denied permissions, framing/recording/audio/countdown, playback/takes, upload/retry, consent renewal and account deletion against the deployed backend. Prior physical tests and emulator deletion checks do not replace this final pass. Test the intended AAB architecture set and 16 KB runtime requirements; the earlier static ELF check is baseline evidence only.')}`);
